@CustomerApp_HostAddress = http://localhost:5300

### English validation messages (HTTP 400)
POST {{CustomerApp_HostAddress}}/api/registrations
Content-Type: application/json
Accept-Language: en

{
  "firstName": "",
  "lastName": "",
  "email": "invalid",
  "inviteCode": ""
}

### Dutch validation messages, including the async invite-code rule (HTTP 400)
POST {{CustomerApp_HostAddress}}/api/registrations
Content-Type: application/json
Accept-Language: nl-NL

{
  "firstName": "",
  "lastName": "",
  "email": "invalid",
  "inviteCode": "NOT-A-CODE"
}

### Query-string culture overrides Accept-Language (English errors, HTTP 400)
POST {{CustomerApp_HostAddress}}/api/registrations?culture=en
Content-Type: application/json
Accept-Language: nl

{
  "firstName": "Test",
  "lastName": "User",
  "email": "test@example.com",
  "inviteCode": "NOT-A-CODE"
}

### Non-consuming availability check (JSON boolean)
POST {{CustomerApp_HostAddress}}/api/invite-codes/validate
Content-Type: application/json

"WELCOME-2026"

### Dutch form labels and validation; reload to change the interactive culture
GET {{CustomerApp_HostAddress}}/register?culture=nl

### English form labels and validation
GET {{CustomerApp_HostAddress}}/register?culture=en
